+# Lesson templates (proposed v0.7 additions)
+
+Three small, additive changes so that short lesson explainers can be built with the studio's fixed templates. Nothing here executes model-authored Python, and without the new optional fields every template generates byte-for-byte the same code as v0.6 (a test checks the SHA-256 of all eight).
+
+| Change | What it does | Where |
+|---|---|---|
+| `Scene.data` | A plain dict of short labels and numbers. Used only by `bars` and `flow`; any other visual type with `data` is rejected | `studio/models.py` |
+| `bars` template (skill `bar-comparison`) | 2 to 6 labelled non-negative numbers as bars, with optional title and unit (`$`, `ms`, `%`). Not offered to the AI planner (`needs_data`) | `studio/animation.py`, `studio/skills.py` |
+| Labelled `flow` | `data.labels` (2 to 4 labels) replaces "Input, Process, Output". Without `data` the old three boxes are unchanged | `studio/animation.py` |
+| Scene length | `duration_seconds` (3 to 90) stretches only the final wait, so the scene lasts about as long as its narration; never shorter than the animation plus 0.5 s | `studio/animation.py` |
+
+Validation is strict and fails closed: labels allow only letters, digits, space and `. , : % $ ( ) / + & -` (quotes, backslashes and non-ASCII text are rejected, not escaped), numbers must be finite and between 0 and 1,000,000,000, and `plan_collaboration` reports every violation before anything renders.
+
+Known limits: labels are ASCII only; `duration_seconds` is an estimate from the template's fixed run times, not a measurement of the narration audio; the narration itself is still not synthesised or aligned.
